{
  "name": "mcp-rust-docs",
  "description": "This Model Context Protocol (MCP) server implementation provides structured access to Rust crate documentation for Large Language Models by fetching and sanitizing content from docs.rs. It utilizes a stdio-based JSON-RPC transport and implements specific HTML-to-plaintext transformations to ensure documentation is both readable and token-efficient for LLM prompts. By exposing a configurable tool interface, it enables AI assistants to autonomously retrieve API references and module definitions during Rust-focused development tasks.",
